-- Adds eb_sessions.bic (nullable — the ASPSP BIC staged at auth initiation,
-- mirroring how `logo` is persisted), accounts.in_consent (NOT NULL DEFAULT 1 —
-- 1 marks an account within the authorization's account filter that the sync
-- runner fetches; 0 marks a kept-as-local-copy account the sync runner skips),
-- and accounts.identification_hash (nullable — Enable Banking's primary
-- cross-session account match key, captured at authorization time alongside
-- the account's other fields; NULL only for accounts authorized before this
-- change and malformed responses). The default 1 is correct for every existing
-- account (all pre-existing accounts are synced accounts); existing rows are
-- untouched.
--
-- SQLite's ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN has no IF NOT EXISTS; this migration only
-- runs when user_version < Schema.version, and the DatabaseFactory inference
-- ladder only classifies a database as being AT or AFTER this version when ALL
-- THREE columns are present (see DatabaseFactory.kt) — so the ALTERs never
-- re-run on an already-migrated database. (Pre-release ruling: databases
-- initialized at the intermediate bic+in_consent state — the previous draft of
-- this migration — are development artifacts and are recreated, not migrated.
-- They can surface through two loud paths, both covered in DatabaseFactory:
-- a user_version = 0 database re-runs this migration and fails loudly on the
-- duplicate bic ALTER; a database stamped at Schema.version bypasses the
-- ladder and is caught by the boot-time column sanity check, which exits
-- loudly with the recreate instruction — never a deferred merge crash.)
ALTER TABLE eb_sessions ADD COLUMN bic TEXT;
ALTER TABLE accounts ADD COLUMN in_consent INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;
ALTER TABLE accounts ADD COLUMN identification_hash TEXT;
